{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_source_guides_data_mixing_guide", "label": "Data Mixing guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Guide (text-specific) to the three ways olmo_core mixes sets of pre-tokenized numpy files for training."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_data_mixing_approaches", "label": "Three data-mixing approaches", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "olmo_core offers three ways to mix pre-tokenized numpy files: (1) fine-grained ratio-based sampling via olmo_core.data.source_mixture or the composable mixing classes, (2) predefined catalog-style mixes via olmo_core.data.mixes, and (3) simple path/glob lists passed to NumpyDatasetConfig or NumpyDocumentSource."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_data_mixing_composable_mixing", "label": "Composable ratio-based mixing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The composable API mixes/samples at token- (MixingTokenSource), document- (MixingDocumentSource), or instance-level (MixingInstanceSource). Each source spec carries: source (a TokenSource/DocumentSource/InstanceSource), ratio (relative target ratio), max_repetition_factor (>=1.0; 1.0 means no repetition, 2.0 allows seeing each instance twice), and an optional label for logging. build() yields an InstanceSource for a ComposableDataLoader, optionally wrapped (e.g. SamplingInstanceSource to set instances-per-epoch)."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_data_mixing_source_mixture", "label": "SourceMixture ratio budgeting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One SourceMixtureConfig per source (target_ratio summing to 1.0 across sources; paths of .npy files; max_repetition_ratio>1.0 upsamples a small source; max_source_fraction caps how much of a source is consumed to leave hold-out data). Wrapped in SourceMixtureDatasetConfig (requested_tokens, global_batch_size which must be a multiple of sequence_length, processes for parallel size-scanning, seed for deterministic rounding, render_tables/quiet), it counts tokens, applies the Hamilton apportionment scheme to keep ratios precise, logs summary tables, and supplies file weights to NumpyFSLDatasetMixture. Unmet ratios (source too small, repetition disabled) raise OLMoConfigurationError. Currently only compatible with NumpyFSLDatasetMixture (no padding/packing/VSL)."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_data_mixing_predefined_mixes", "label": "Predefined data mixes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The DataMix enum encodes text manifests (.txt with label,path rows) listing shard labels and relative paths (e.g. OLMoE_mix_0824). When mix is set, NumpyFSLDatasetConfig loads the manifest, patches the {TOKENIZER} placeholder to the active tokenizer identifier (special cases per TokenizerName), and injects shard labels into metadata; you only supply the base location (S3 prefix or shared filesystem). Extend the catalog by subclassing DataMixBase, adding an enum value, and providing a matching .txt manifest under olmo_core/data/mixes."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_data_mixing_simple_globs", "label": "Simple path/glob lists", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The most direct option points NumpyFSLDatasetConfig at an explicit list of token files (paths), ideal when data lives in one directory or should be treated uniformly. Use glob patterns via expand_glob=True or the glob() constructor (which defers expansion to build() so validation happens at startup). label_mask_paths supply matching numpy boolean per-token loss masks; metadata provides per-path dicts returned with each instance when include_instance_metadata=True (the default)."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_data_mixing_choosing", "label": "Choosing a mixing approach", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use fine-grained source mixtures when you need deterministic token budgets, custom repetition logic, or transparent ratio auditing; reach for predefined mixes when an existing manifest captures the blend or you prefer declarative management without code; use simple path lists for one-off experiments or small datasets."}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable_tokensource", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable.TokenSource", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable_documentsource", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable.DocumentSource", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable_mixingtokensource", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable.MixingTokenSource", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable_mixingdocumentsource", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable.MixingDocumentSource", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable_mixinginstancesource", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable.MixingInstanceSource", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable_concatandchunkinstancesource", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable.ConcatAndChunkInstanceSource", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable_samplinginstancesource", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable.SamplingInstanceSource", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_composable_numpydocumentsource", "label": "olmo_core.data.composable.NumpyDocumentSource", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_data_source_mixture", "label": "olmo_core.data.source_mixture", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/data_mixing.rst", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_da